// A `for` OVER A NAMED ARRAY OR SLICE OF OWNERS HOLDS A VIEW OF THAT PLACE FOR ITS BODY (DEF-421, landing 177b; `push_for_place_party`, alias.npk). The binding is a shallow copy of each element
// (`emit_for_indexed`), so a write-capable access AT the place, ABOVE it or BELOW it -- an element or whole-array store, a store through a held address or pointer, a callee handed `@o` or `self`, a `$$m`
// claim, a prefix `o = …`/`o.i = …`, an element's `list_push(@a[0], …)` -- is `NITPICK-BORROW-015` for the loop's frame. Every refused cell read FREED bytes on 175, 176b and 177a (83: the first byte of a
// freed string; 140: a freed `List` body) or was a leak masking one (`s1_slice_param_write`, 67: a store through a plain slice never drops the old owner, DEF-422). A binding, a field, an element, a
// dereference, a pointer parameter's pointee, a parenthesised place, a `self` field and a generic `T[2]` (an unbounded `T` counts as dropping) are one road. OVER-REFUSED ON PURPOSE, THE POST-180 LIST:
// a write in a `defer` body (`fa_defer`), a dead write after the last read (`fa_dead_write`), another element written (`fa_other_elem`: the next iteration binds it), a `T: Copy` element (`e3d_copy_param`:
// the pass reads no bound; management_13's closed choice, 2026-11-01 16:07). The legal twins are `tests/backend/programs/for_array_owner_ok.npk`. The cells: `.internal/probes177b/cells421*/`,
// `MANAGEMENT/probes/177-review-c/` (the row's), `MANAGEMENT/probes/177b-def421/` (management_13's); the results `.internal/probes177b/out421_1/`.
